%description:
Tests an ICMP fragmentation-needed error for a SYN without data in SYN_SENT
(pmtudEnabled). The path answers the SYN (A001) with the error for an MTU of
800, and the client lowers its MSS to 760. It does not retransmit at once: a
SYN without data is not larger than the new MSS, so it waits for its timer, as
Linux does. The SYN of the timer (A002, t=3 s) announces an MSS of 760, and the
data later goes in segments of 760 bytes.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 10s
*.cli_app.sendScript="4.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1460
*.cli_tcp.pmtudEnabled = true
*.tcptester.script="a1 icmp 3 4 mtu 800"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# answering with an ICMP error
[3.001 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[3.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S 750500:750500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[3.005 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 750501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[4.001 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:761(760) ack 750501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
PMTUD: reducing snd_mss from 1460 to 760 (reported MTU=800)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Tcp Header Option MSS(=760) sent
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%not-contains: stdout
retransmitting a bare SYN at once
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
